<body>
    <h1>Access Control in the UI</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h1 id=3D"AccessControlintheUI-Designconstraints"><br>
  Design constraints</h1>
<p><br>
  We were required to control access to the UI via a combination of "resour=
ces" and "scopes".&nbsp; For any feature which is access-controlled, both r=
esources and scopes would be declared, and a user would require to have all=
 "resources" and "scopes" necessary in order to access.&nbsp;<br><br>
  "Resources" are for product defined features within the UI which they wan=
ted to control access to features not governed by permission.</p>
<p>"Permissions (derived via Scopes)" are for BCM aligned access control.<b=
r><br>
  The only endpoints available for checking whether or not the user had acc=
ess to a "resource" or a "permission" are via the endpoints <span style=3D"=
color:#172b4d;">G12&nbsp;</span>and R9 in the <a href=3D"/spaces/NBINDM/pag=
es/2254868289/Authorization+API">Authorization API</a>.<br><br>
  The Loading of the UI application requires Access to be verified before l=
oading or rendering of the access-controlled features.<br>
  The Loading and Rendering of the UI is generally expected to be less than=
 1 second.</p>
<p>The UI has various UI micro front-ends, and the access-control behaviour=
 needs to be the same across the entire UI experience.</p>
<h2 id=3D"AccessControlintheUI-TypeofAccessControl:"><br>
  Type of Access Control:</h2>
<p><strong>Navigation Access Control</strong></p>
<p>We need to control access to loading a page when entered via the URL, or=
 attempting to access via a Hyperlink or click through navigation.<br><br><=
span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-s=
ize"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" height=3D=
"319" src=3D"7c443e145ef4a64d397260968f4a48a9172d380b9d3b70fd07b62137804f89=
54" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/1367484275/Screen%20Shot%202022=
